id: core/objective-holon
title: "objective holons and Yawn.bot activation"
kind: ontology-contract
status: draft-0.1
updated: 2026-08-25

definition: >
  A principal-owned objective may become its own Yawn holon when it deserves a
  persistent orientation, authority, relationship, question, and proof loop. A
  Yawn.bot is the bounded stewarding agent bound to that contract; it is not the
  objective, the principal, or the Yawn itself.

lifecycle:
  - source-preserved-signal
  - typed-detections
  - objective-candidate
  - structural-routing-proposal
  - principal-ratification
  - objective-holding-yawn
  - sleeping-yawn-bot
  - explicit-activation-grant
  - turns-moves-proof-and-replay

distinct_records:
  objective_candidate: "machine-attributed hypothesis; never silently adopted"
  objective: "principal-ratified direction held across goals or turns"
  yawn: "durable orientation contract holding the objective and live lacuna"
  yawn_bot: "bounded stewarding runtime operating inside the Yawn"

root_alignment_bridge:
  role: "detect, route, relate, protect, and propose"
  does_not: "execute every objective or silently authorize descendants"

child_activation_rule: >
  A child bot begins sleeping. Structural context may be proposed for
  inheritance, but truth, identity, consent, privacy, confidence, proof, and
  effect authority require their own attributed records or explicit grants.

bot_roles:
  - root_steward
  - objective_steward
  - worker

invariants:
  - "Detection is not ratification."
  - "Ratification is not effect authority."
  - "A Yawn is the contract; a Yawn.bot is its bounded steward."
  - "One objective steward has one ratified primary objective."
  - "An ongoing objective can gather local proof without claiming final proof of identity or worth."
  - "Duplication copies a protocol shell, never authority, consent, truth, or proof."
  - "Personality is optional programmed projection data, not default bot identity."

links:
  - spec/objective-holons.md
  - schemas/objective-holon.v0.1.schema.json
  - interface/objective-compiler.yawn
  - examples/dave-good-dad-objective-holon.yawn
